---@class posthog.messaging_supabase_auth_emails.UpdateMessagingSupabaseAuthEmailsSettingsPartialRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field supabase_url? string The Supabase project URL, such as https://abcdefgh.supabase.co, from the project's API settings in the Supabase dashboard. It must use https.
---@field hook_secret? string|distilled.Secret The Send Email Hook secret, starting with v1,whsec_. Supabase generates it under Authentication, Hooks, Send Email hook. Leave it out to keep the stored secret.
---@field templates? posthog.messaging_supabase_auth_emails.UpdateMessagingSupabaseAuthEmailsSettingsPartialRequestTemplatesMap Supabase email action type to the id of the email template that sends it. Each template must be transactional and marked sensitive. This replaces the whole mapping: include every type to keep, and leave a type out to unmap it. A core auth email with no template fails in Supabase, and a notification with no template is skipped. Valid action types: signup, invite, magiclink, email, recovery, email_change, reauthentication, password_changed_notification, email_changed_notification, phone_changed_notification, identity_linked_notification, identity_unlinked_notification, mfa_factor_enrolled_notification, mfa_factor_unenrolled_notification.

